### Godot version

4.0 alpha 3

### System information

Windows 11, AMD RX 6700XT, Vulkan, Driver Version 22.2.3

### Issue description

When writing a custom spatial shader if I add any uniforms I get this warning. The shader still works fine in both the editor and the game. I haven't touched any limits in the project settings. It seems like it is not properly determining my device limits? I am assuming because of the -1.

`Line 2 (DEVICE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED):The total size of the uniform buffer for this shader on this device has been exceeded (4/-1). The shader may not work correctly.`

### Steps to reproduce

add any uniform to a shader

``` glsl
shader_type spatial;

uniform float test = 0.0f;

void fragment() {
	// Place fragment code here.
}
